WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:16.555
On Saturday afternoon Tom and Huck pushed open the creaky door of the haunted house.

2
00:00:16.556 --> 00:00:18.697
The house was very quiet.

3
00:00:18.698 --> 00:00:22.846
In the cracks of the stone floor, sickly looking weeds were growing.

4
00:00:22.847 --> 00:00:27.850
The stone fireplace was crumbling, and cobwebs hung from every corner.

5
00:00:27.851 --> 00:00:33.788
"See," whispered Tom, "haunted houses aren't so bad during the day."

6
00:00:33.789 --> 00:00:35.340
Huck only nodded.

7
00:00:35.341 --> 00:00:40.406
The boys left their tools by the fireplace, and Tom led Huck up the stairs.

8
00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:46.178
The stairs were old and rotten in many places, but the boys had no problem climbing them.

9
00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:50.967
The boys searched a closet for hidden treasure but they found nothing.

10
00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:57.590
Huck was getting ready to go down the stairs when Tom hissed, "Shhh . . . Listen!"

11
00:00:57.591 --> 00:01:00.775
"Wh . . . what is it?" asked Huck.

12
00:01:00.776 --> 00:01:05.744
"Someone's coming," whispered Tom. The boys looked at each other in fear.

13
00:01:05.745 --> 00:01:08.115
Then they lay flat on the floor.

14
00:01:08.116 --> 00:01:11.703
Each peered through a knothole in the floorboards.

15
00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:14.044
Two men entered the room below.

16
00:01:14.045 --> 00:01:18.062
One was a Spaniard whom the boys had seen around town.

17
00:01:18.063 --> 00:01:21.926
The boys had never seen the other man before.

18
00:01:21.927 --> 00:01:29.022
The men talked in whispers as they entered the house, but once they shut the door, they began to speak at normal volume.

19
00:01:29.023 --> 00:01:33.736
"It's dangerous," said the ugly unshaven man to the Spaniard.

20
00:01:33.737 --> 00:01:39.287
"Dangerous?" echoed the Spaniard. "I don't care. I want revenge."

21
00:01:39.288 --> 00:01:41.925
The boys began to shake with fear.

22
00:01:41.926 --> 00:01:47.459
The voice of the Spaniard was Injun Joe's!

23
00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:54.295
Tom and Huck were both sure that when Injun Joe said "revenge," he meant he wanted to get revenge on them.

24
00:01:54.296 --> 00:01:57.635
"I think it's dangerous," argued the other man.

25
00:01:57.636 --> 00:02:02.110
"If you don't want to help," said Injun Joe, "you can wait for me up the river.

26
00:02:02.111 --> 00:02:05.395
I'll do the job, and then we'll be off to Texas."

27
00:02:05.396 --> 00:02:13.307
"I said I was your partner," said the ugly man, "so I'll help. I just wish we could have done it—"

28
00:02:13.308 --> 00:02:16.060
"I know," interrupted Injun Joe.

29
00:02:16.061 --> 00:02:21.791
"Those darn kids were playing right outside the whole day, so we couldn't have left this house without being seen."

30
00:02:21.792 --> 00:02:27.276
"Have you got any food in your sack?" asked the man. "I'm starving."

31
00:02:27.277 --> 00:02:32.965
Injun Joe pulled some food out of his very large and very heavy sack, and the two men had lunch.

32
00:02:32.966 --> 00:02:34.813
Then they fell asleep.

33
00:02:34.814 --> 00:02:40.349
Tom and Huck started for the stairs, but the floorboards creaked and moaned with every step.

34
00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:46.062
They worried that the sleeping men would wake up, so they decided to remain upstairs.

35
00:02:46.063 --> 00:02:51.075
Injun Joe woke first, and then he woke his partner. "It's almost time."

36
00:02:51.076 --> 00:02:56.350
"Okay," said the ugly man with a yawn. "But shouldn't we hide our loot here?

37
00:02:56.351 --> 00:03:00.608
Six hundred and fifty dollars in silver is a lot to carry."

38
00:03:00.609 --> 00:03:04.599
"You're right," said Injun Joe. "Let's bury it deep."

39
00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:09.836
Injun Joe pulled out his knife and began to dig in the dirt under the rotten floorboards.

40
00:03:09.837 --> 00:03:13.139
It wasn't long before Joe's knife struck something.

41
00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:15.997
"What did you hit?" asked his partner.

42
00:03:15.998 --> 00:03:20.248
"I'm not sure, but I think it's a box," said Injun Joe.

43
00:03:20.249 --> 00:03:25.046
He reached his hand into the box and pulled out a handful of gold coins.

44
00:03:25.047 --> 00:03:30.846
Everyone in the house—the two men and the two boys—stared at the money.

45
00:03:30.847 --> 00:03:33.855
"I saw a pick in the corner by the fireplace.

46
00:03:33.856 --> 00:03:37.755
Let's find out how much there is," said the man excitedly.

47
00:03:37.756 --> 00:03:42.715
He grabbed the boys' pick, and Injun Joe used it to dig up the box.

48
00:03:42.716 --> 00:03:48.589
"There's over ten-thousand dollars here," said Injun Joe. "We're rich!"

49
00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:52.288
"You won't need to do that other job now," said the other man.

50
00:03:52.289 --> 00:03:57.990
Injun Joe frowned and said, "It isn't just a robbery, it's also revenge.

51
00:03:57.991 --> 00:04:01.081
As soon as we're finished we'll go to Texas."

52
00:04:01.082 --> 00:04:05.809
"Okay," said the man. "The sooner we get the job done, the better.

53
00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:07.952
Should we bury the money again?"

54
00:04:07.953 --> 00:04:10.198
Injun Joe looked at the pick.

55
00:04:10.199 --> 00:04:14.558
"What's this doing here? It wasn't here yesterday," he said.

56
00:04:14.559 --> 00:04:18.985
The two men looked at each other, and then Injun Joe pointed to the ceiling.

57
00:04:18.986 --> 00:04:22.611
Right away the boys knew they were going to die.

58
00:04:22.612 --> 00:04:26.079
Injun Joe grabbed his knife and began to climb the stairs.

59
00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:31.726
The boys were sliding across the floor toward the closet when the stairs made a terrible groaning noise.

60
00:04:31.727 --> 00:04:35.536
Then the stairs crashed down in a cloud of dust.

61
00:04:35.537 --> 00:04:38.262
Injun Joe was furious.

62
00:04:38.263 --> 00:04:43.301
When he got up from the collapsed stairs, his partner reminded him it was time to move out.

63
00:04:43.302 --> 00:04:46.773
"We'll be taking the treasure with us," said Injun Joe.

64
00:04:46.774 --> 00:04:49.646
"Naturally," said the man.

65
00:04:49.647 --> 00:04:56.897
"We'll take it to my hiding place and bury it in number two under the cross," said Injun Joe as they left.

66
00:04:56.898 --> 00:04:59.929
The boys were both happy and sad.

67
00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:06.207
They were happy to be alive but depressed at having lost a chance to get ten-thousand dollars.

68
00:05:06.208 --> 00:05:11.993
"We need to keep an eye out for Injun Joe," said Tom. Huck agreed.

69
00:05:11.994 --> 00:05:18.262
"If he comes into town, we should follow him to hiding place number two," Tom added.

70
00:05:18.263 --> 00:05:24.767
Then Tom and Huck walked back to town, dreaming of being rich.
